\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. Hark the glad sound! the Saviour comes,
\par The Saviour promised long;
\par Let every heart prepare a throne,
\par And every voice a song.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. He comes the prisoners to release,
\par In Satan's bondage held;
\par The gates of brass before Him burst,
\par The iron fetters yield.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. He comes the broken heart to bind,
\par The bleeding soul to cure,
\par And with the teasures of His grace
\par To enrich the humble poor.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. Our glad hasannas, Prince of Peace,
\par Thy welcome shall proclaim,
\par And heaven's eternal arches ring,
\par With Thy beloved name.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\fs16 
\par }

